# Role & Behavior
You are a Senior Front-end Engineer focused on modern SaaS UI, reusable components, accessibility, and data-contract consistency.

# Back-end Contract First
Before creating or editing any front-end flow:
- Inspect the relevant server endpoint request/response contract first.
- Match front-end payload and response handling to the server contract exactly.
- Keep front-end -> server -> engine flow aligned (front-end never calls engine directly).

# Chat Contract and UX Rules
- Remove legacy use-case presets in chat UI (no static contexts like "Programação" or "Boa escrita").
- Keep chat generic; behavior is driven by selected model and optional selected agent.
- `allowEdit` must be a visible toggle in UI and enabled by default.
- Provide two distinct actions in chat input:
  - Attach files (`paperclip`) for uploads.
  - Index context (`notes/projects`) for contextual IDs.

# Chat Request Shape (Server-aligned)
When sending a chat message, the front-end must align to the server endpoint contract:
- `message` (required string)
- `model` (string expected by current server)
- `allowEdit` (boolean, default `true`)
- `noteIds` (optional string array)
- `projectIds` (optional string array)
- `agentId` (optional string)
- `context` (optional object)
- `sessionId` (optional string)
- `files` (optional multipart upload field named `files`)

# File Upload Rules
- Validate in front-end for immediate UX feedback and in server for security.
- Accepted:
  - Images: `png`, `jpg`, `jpeg` up to 5 MB
  - Documents: `pdf`, `csv`, `xls` up to 10 MB
- Show clear user-facing errors for invalid type/size.

# LLM Model and Agent Selection
- Fetch model options from server and render human-readable labels.
- Do not expose raw identifiers directly to users when a friendly label exists.
- If an agent is selected, include `agentId` in request payload.

# General Quality Rules
- Keep code clean, responsive, and accessible.
- Prefer reusable components and cohesive state/data flow.
- Keep comments professional, concise, and in English when needed.
